SUMMARY:The Kavanaghs: Married With Parents
LOCATION:Town Hall Theatre\, Galway
DESCRIPTION:They’re living in despair (room). A hilarious new Irish comed
 y about Generation Stuck – the adults who thought they’d only be living
  with their parents for a few months… until life got in the way. Packed w
 ith big laughs\, family chaos and razor-sharp observations\, The Kavanaghs:
  Married with Parents is a brand new farce from Al Porter and Karl Spain. A
 l and Ryan only moved back in with his parents for six months. That was six
  years ago. Now\, with Al’s parents preparing to fly to Germany for a wed
 ding\, the happy couple are finally about to have the house to themselves
 … or so they think. As suitcases pile up\, secrets unravel and unexpected
  guests keep arriving\, one ordinary weekend in Tallaght spirals into glori
 ous chaos in this fast-paced comedy about family\, love and the generation 
 that can’t quite leave home. Starring Aisling O’Neill (Fair City’s Ca
 rol)\, Phelim Drew (Once\, Remembering Ronnie)\, Al Porter (Perrier nominee
 )\, Ryan Andrews (Fair City) and top comics Willa White and Enya Mar\nMore 
